<style>
    table, th, td {
    border:2px solid black;
    border-collapse:COLLAPSE;
    }
    th, td{
        padding: 15px;
    }
    th{
    text-align:center;
    border: 5px solid black;
    }
</style>
<body >
    <h1 style= "text-align: center;">HYPERTEXT MARKUP LANGUAGE (HTML) TABLE</h1>
    <h2>An HTML TABLE is crwated using the (table)tag, which arranges structure data into rows and columns.</h2>
    <h3>CORE HTML TABLE TAGS:</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>table: Enclose the entire table data structure</li>
        <li>tr : Defines a single horizontal TABLE ROW</li>
        <li>th : Sets a TABLE HEADER(th) cell. </li>
        <li>td : Specifies a standard TABLE DATA(td) </li>
    </ol>
    <h3>SEMATIC STRUCTURAL ELEMENTS</h3>
    <h4>For larger or complex datasets, use semantic tags to group your structural sections:</h4>
    <ol>
        <li> caption : Places a descriptive title directly above the table layout.</li>
        <li>thead : Wraps the master header rows of your dataset.</li>
        <li>tbody : Groups the primary body content containing data rows.</li>
        <li> tfoot : Encloses summary or total rows at the bottom</li>
    </ol>
    <h3>SPANNING LAYOUT ATTRIBUTES</h3>
    <OL>
        <li>colspan: Streches a data cell horizontally across multiple columns</li>
        <li>rowspan: Extends a single cell vertically down across multiple rows</li>
      </OL>
    <table style="width:100%">
    <tr bgcolor="lightblue">
        <th width="333.333">HEALTH RISKS OF WORKING AT THE COMPUTER</th>
        <th width="333.333">ECONOMIC TIPS FOR COMPUTER USERS</th>
        <th width="333.333">SIGNS OF POOR ERGONOMICS</th>
        
    </tr>
    <tr align="center">
         <td>Musculoskeletal Problems</td>
        <td>Proper Sitting Posture</td>
        <td>Back Pain</td>
        </tr>
        <tr align="center">
            <td>Repetitive Strain Injury (RSI) </td>
            <td>Correct Monitor Placement</td>
            <td>Neck Stiffness</td>
        <tr align="center">
        <td>Computer Vision Syndrom (CVS) </td>
        <td>Proper Keyboard & Mouse Position</td>
        <td>Eye discomfort</td>
        <tr align="center">
        <td>Mental Fatigue and Stress</td>
        <td>Stretching Exercises</td>
        <td>Wrist pain</td>
        <tr align="center">
        <td>Sedentary Lifestyle Risks</td>
        <td>Taking breaks</td>
        <td>Headaches</td>
        <tr align="center">
        <td>Long-Term Health Risks</td>
        <td>Healthy Computer Habits</td>
        <td>Fatigue</td>
                 
    </tr>
    
    
    
    
    
    </table>
</body>
</html>